.policy "ruff-dtz011-call-date-today" revision 2
.description "Derive today's date from a timezone-aware current datetime instead of the naive local date; the local date depends on the machine's timezone."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff DTZ011 (flake8-datetimez): `datetime.date.today()`, the date in the machine's local timezone. Ruff
// reports it even when `.astimezone` follows. Reported at the call. Only in a file that imports datetime.
//   datetime.date.today()                        ← DTZ011
//   from datetime import date; date.today()      ← DTZ011
#include "python/datetime.rr"

.violation DTZ011(at: node) code "DTZ011"
    "Use `datetime.datetime.now(tz=...).date()` with the timezone whose calendar date you need; `date.today()` is the naive local date, so keep it only if that is intended."
    suppress ruff "DTZ011"
DTZ011(c) :- dt_call(c, "datetime.date.today").
